 "checkpoint": "Corsica and Sardinia Held",
 "note": "From a save. Al-Andalus holds seven Corsican towns (Aleria, Calvi, Corte, Ajaccio, Bonifacio, Sartène, Vico) and five of Arborea's in Sardinia (Oristano, Ales, Sorgono, Terralba, Thiesi); Bastia is under siege. The allies' attacks on Palermo itself have failed four times, and Gabès left the war in December. Aḥmad, lord of Banbalūna, died of camp fever on campaign (18 February 1449) and his son succeeded him. In the Mamlūks' war on the Banū Lām, in which al-Andalus has not fought, the Mamlūk side has lost most of its battles in the Ḥijāz and Najd. Further north, Bohemia's war for the Hungarian throne (from September 1447) has overrun eastern Hungary. Stability 19.3, political influence at its cap of 100, prestige 93; treasury 175. Since October 1447: gunsmiths at Jaén and Santarém, tanneries at Córdoba, masons, scriptoria, distilleries, potteries, a paper mill at Lleida, a bridge at Vielha, and the Jamāʿa's urban seat at al-Ushbūna. Estate power estimated from the reading of 16 November 1428.",
